.TH FBARCALC 1
.SH NAME
.B fbarcalc
- help to calculate your maximum account value

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbarcalc
[config]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbarcalc
is a tool that helps you to calculate the maximum account value in an account
so that you can determine if you need to submit an FBAR and what the
associated value is.

With an account's starting balance and a list of transactions you input them
one-by one and the program will keep track of whatever the maximum value
reached is. At the end the final balance is shown too, so that it can be
compared with the statement that the transactions came from to make sure that
they were all entered correctly.

We presume that we're working with a foreign currency given that we're working
on the FBAR so the input should be in the original currency and at the end of
the input the program will return the value in USD.

.RS
Currently supported currencies:
.nf
- Euro (EUR: €)
- British Pound Sterling (GBP: £)
- Japanese Yen (JPY: ¥)
- US Dollar (USD: $)
.fi
.RE

You'll need an API key from
.BI freecurrencyapi.com
in order to perform the conversion, unless the input currency is USD. The free
tier is quite generous and should be more than enough for personal use.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Provide a custom configuration file. This can be used with the
.BR config
command too.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show the balance after each transaction, with the maximum marked, and the
exchange rate that was used for the conversion, so that the result can be
checked. This applies to the calculation and not to the
.BR config
command.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Prints help menu.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Prints the program version.

